    {
      "id": "background",
      "navLabel": "Background",
      "title": "Historical Background",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "context",
          "heading": "The City of Ephesus",
          "body": [
            {
              "p": "<strong>Location:</strong> Ephesus was the capital city of the Roman province of Asia (modern-day Turkey), strategically located on the Aegean Sea. It was one of the largest cities in the Roman Empire, with a population of around 250,000-500,000 people."
            },
            {
              "p": "<strong>Economic Status:</strong> A major commercial and trade center, Ephesus was incredibly wealthy. The city was famous for its magnificent harbor, extensive road systems, and as a center of banking and commerce."
            },
            {
              "p": "<strong>Religious Climate:</strong> Ephesus was home to the Temple of Artemis (Diana), one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World. The city was a center of pagan worship, magic practices, and emperor worship, making it a challenging environment for Christian witness."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "themes",
          "heading": "Paul's Relationship with Ephesus",
          "body": [
            {
              "p": "<strong>Extended Ministry:</strong> Paul spent approximately three years in Ephesus (Acts 19:8-10, 20:31), his longest recorded ministry in any single location. This deep relationship is evident in the emotional farewell recorded in Acts 20:17-38."
            },
            {
              "ul": [
                "<strong>Church Planting:</strong> Established a strong, influential church",
                "<strong>Training Center:</strong> Taught daily in the school of Tyrannus",
                "<strong>Regional Impact:</strong> Ministry spread throughout Asia Minor",
                "<strong>Miraculous Ministry:</strong> Extraordinary miracles occurred (Acts 19:11-12)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "warning",
          "heading": "Challenges Facing the Ephesian Church",
          "body": [
            {
              "h4": "Spiritual Warfare:"
            },
            {
              "ul": [
                "Surrounded by pagan temples and practices",
                "Magic and occult practices were common",
                "Demonic opposition was real and active"
              ]
            },
            {
              "h4": "Cultural Pressures:"
            },
            {
              "ul": [
                "Emperor worship was mandatory",
                "Guild system created economic pressures",
                "Greek philosophical influences"
              ]
            },
            {
              "h4": "Internal Church Issues:"
            },
            {
              "ul": [
                "Jewish-Gentile tensions over unity",
                "Questions about Christian behavior",
                "Need for spiritual maturity and leadership"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "application",
          "heading": "Modern Parallels",
          "body": [
            {
              "p": "Today's believers face similar challenges:"
            },
            {
              "ul": [
                "<strong>Secular Worldview:</strong> Materialism and humanism",
                "<strong>Spiritual Opposition:</strong> New Age practices and occultism",
                "<strong>Cultural Diversity:</strong> Unity across ethnic and cultural lines",
                "<strong>Moral Relativism:</strong> Pressure to compromise biblical standards",
                "<strong>Economic Pressures:</strong> Career vs. faith conflicts"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "reflection",
          "heading": "Reflection Questions",
          "questions": [
            {
              "audience": "Personal",
              "text": "What cultural pressures in your environment most challenge your Christian walk?"
            },
            {
              "audience": "Group Discussion",
              "text": "How can we create unity in our diverse church communities like the Ephesians needed to do?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "notes",
          "heading": "Your Notes on Background",
          "id": "notes-background-1",
          "placeholder": "Write your observations, questions, or insights about the historical background..."
        },
        {
          "type": "checklist",
          "heading": "Background Study Checklist",
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "bgGoal1",
              "text": "Understand the cultural and religious context of Ephesus"
            },
            {
              "id": "bgGoal2",
              "text": "Recognize Paul's deep relationship with the Ephesian church"
            },
            {
              "id": "bgGoal3",
              "text": "Identify challenges facing early Christians in Ephesus"
            },
            {
              "id": "bgGoal4",
              "text": "Reflect on modern parallels to these challenges"
            }
          ],
          "badge": {
            "id": "bgBadge",
            "text": "Section Completed!"
          }
        }
      ]
